_:Ndde43220f9a040fd99eba35b122ea2cb <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasOutput> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Flow> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasInput> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Verbindet einen Prozessoperator mit einem in ihn eingehenden Fluss."@de .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Energy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Energy required or released by a process operator, for example electrical energy or heat."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#TechnicalResource> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Product> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "VDI 3682 Part 1, Section 4.1, page 8. A product is not a kind of state: it has one, which hasState records. The thing and the condition it is in are kept apart, so the same sheet of metal before and after a stamping is one product in two states."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasState> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Used in two places. A flow carries a state, and a product, an energy or an information has one. The thing is therefore separate from the condition it is in, which is what lets one product appear in a process before and after a transformation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "1.0.0" .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#TechnicalResource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Physische Komponenten, aus denen automatisierte Anlagen aufgebaut sind und die die Umwandlungen der Produkte durch Prozessoperatoren realisieren."@de .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-09-02"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
